## 4. The final correction that still lacks an independent check

### 4.1 Which one

**The load-order clauses of the permission corrections**
(`docs/runs/mod-permission-review-corrections-2026-10-29.md:13-19`):

> "Each public load now starts from reset registries, retaining the configured source
> order while removing old bodies, settings, helper methods and basket entries. An
> explicit empty order remains empty instead of falling back to all available sources.
> Invalid order resolution validates its names before replacing the prior order."

Clause-by-clause control coverage in the committed suite:

| Clause | Committed control | Status |
|---|---|---|
| explicit empty order stays empty | `view-permission-settings.test.ts:26-30` | covered |
| invalid order raises on an unknown name | `mod-load-order.test.ts:139-146` | covered |
| **the prior order survives a failed resolveOrder** ("before replacing the prior order") | — | **not covered** |
| removes old bodies / settings / view chain | `view-permission-settings.test.ts:12-31`, `card-mod-assets.test.ts:302-319` | covered |
| **removes old helper methods** | — | **not covered** |
| **removes old basket entries** | — | **not covered** |

`mod-load-order.test.ts:139-146` asserts only that `resolveOrder` throws
`"mod not found: missing"`. It never sets a valid order, attempts an invalid
resolution, and then asserts that the prior order survived. The committed reload
controls cover bodies, settings and the view chain; `formatMethodLookup`,
`basketTaskEntries` and `basketWarningEntries` have no reload control.

**Compounding this:** the corrections doc's own cited evidence
(`.runtime/adversarial-repair/mod-denial-corrections-tests-final.log` and
`mod-denial-corrections-final-noemit.log`, doc lines 42-43) **does not exist in this
